---
title: "dynamic_field::add (Sui Move Concepts: Dynamic Fields)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_get_addr: object_addr = object.to_address()
    q_get_addr --> q_hash: hash = hash_type_and_key(object_addr, name)
    q_hash --> q_check_exists: check has_child_object(object_addr, hash)
    q_check_exists --> q_abort: field already exists
    q_check_exists --> q_create_field: field does not exist
    q_create_field --> q_set_field: Field { id: new_uid_from_hash(hash), name, value }
    q_set_field --> [*]: add_child_object(object_addr, field)

    q_abort --> [*]: abort EFieldAlreadyExists

    note right of q_hash
        INV-001: Field identity is determined by hash of (parent_addr, type, key)
        INV-002: Hash is deterministic for same parent + name combination
    end note

    note right of q_check_exists
        INV-003: Duplicate field names (same type + value) are rejected
        INV-004: Fields with different Name types but same value are distinct
    end note

    note right of q_set_field
        INV-005: Field UID is derived from hash, not randomly generated
        INV-006: Value with store ability can be any type (dynamic_field)
        INV-007: Value with key + store required for dynamic_object_field
    end note
